A patch of the Odin compiler (release dev-2026-11a, pinned in flake.nix).
flake.nix applies it to the compiler of the development shell and of the
checks.

The fault. `-thread-count:1` does not give one thread. src/main.cpp,
init_global_thread_pool, makes `worker_count = thread_count` workers beside
the main thread ("// +1"). With `-thread-count:1` the pool has two threads.

The correction. `-thread-count:N` means N threads in all: the main thread and
N-1 workers, as the backend already counts (lb_generate_code). With
`-thread-count:1` no worker exists: the main thread runs each task, in one
order.

diff --git i/src/main.cpp w/src/main.cpp
index 14fde3c..c8df8ba 100644
--- i/src/main.cpp
+++ w/src/main.cpp
@@ -15,7 +15,11 @@
 #include "build_settings.cpp"
 gb_internal void init_global_thread_pool(void) {
 	isize thread_count = gb_max(build_context.thread_count, 1);
-	isize worker_count = thread_count; // +1
+	// -thread-count:N means N threads in all: the main thread and N-1 workers,
+	// as in the backend. With -thread-count:1 no worker exists, the main
+	// thread runs each task, and the order of the work is the same at each
+	// build: the same source gives the same output.
+	isize worker_count = thread_count - 1;
 	thread_pool_init(&global_thread_pool, worker_count, "ThreadPoolWorker");
 }
 
